      "restoredAt": null,
      "sourceFeatureExtractionItemID": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I know there is a workaround to access IK syncing for a limited number of parameters using the expression parameters and puppet wheels, but it is limited to 8 parameters at any given time and you have to have a radial menu open on each hand for it to work which is a pain.\n\nIf there were an option to simply set a parameter to IK sync (perhaps with a limited number of parameters), or possibly just have some built into the sdk based off of unified expressions as it is more robust and universal than arkit or sranpai that would be amazing.\n\nOtherwise the common solution is to do interpolation in the animation layers based with a much slower sync rate of playable sync parameters, which is lethargically slow.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
